# Build-context filter for packaging/docker/Dockerfile.ci (BuildKit picks up
# "<dockerfile>.dockerignore" in preference to the repo-root .dockerignore).
#
# It exists to make ONE deliberate exception to the root filter: the CI image
# KEEPS .git.
#
# The root .dockerignore drops .git — right for the e2e rig, wrong here. Parts of
# the stack read real git metadata, so without history they fail in ways that look
# like product bugs (all three found 2026-07-12 by running test-all.sh in the
# container while the host was green):
#   - dashboard "stale code rev": src/git.ts shells out to `git rev-parse HEAD` on
#     the repo root to decide whether a listening arbiter is running old code;
#   - launcher golden-path + fs-preload-live: both seed a symbolized AgentView
#     git worktree of the repo.
# CI must reproduce the shell runner, which has a normal checkout — so: .git stays.
# Cost is ~53 MB of build context, and it does not slow the cached path: the layer
# it lands in (COPY . .) is invalidated by any source edit anyway.
#
# Everything else mirrors the root filter: deps are installed inside the image, and
# nothing secret or host-generated may leak into a layer.
**/node_modules
interceptors/target
eval/agentdojo/.venv

# secrets / host-session artifacts (gitignored, but docker build reads the working
# tree — exclude them explicitly)
secrets.local.json
secrets.json
.env
.mcp.json

# The maintainers' private tree: nothing in the image's build or its test kinds
# needs it, so the container tests what the public export holds, and no private
# file (nor an unreadable tool output under it, which fails the whole context
# load) reaches the build context.
private/
